+# Static IPFS Deployment
+
+These commands build the static artifact and show how to upload it. Do not run the upload commands until you are ready to publish.
+
+## Build
+
+Use the local Base fork workflow first so `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts` contains the current local `USDCTipJar` address:
+
+```bash
+yarn fork:base
+yarn deploy
+yarn seed:usdc
+```
+
+In another terminal, create the static build:
+
+```bash
+yarn ipfs
+```
+
+The output directory is:
+
+```bash
+packages/nextjs/out
+```
+
+## Upload
+
+With a local Kubo IPFS node:
+
+```bash
+CID=$(ipfs add -Qr packages/nextjs/out)
+echo "ipfs://$CID"
+echo "https://$CID.ipfs.dweb.link/"
+```
+
+With any pinning provider, upload the directory `packages/nextjs/out` and keep the returned CID.
+
+## Post-Deploy Verification
+
+Use a subdomain gateway for verification so absolute static asset URLs resolve from the CID origin:
+
+```bash
+export CID=replace-with-uploaded-cid
+export URL="https://$CID.ipfs.dweb.link"
+curl -I "$URL/"
+curl -fsSL "$URL/" | grep -q "USDC Tip Jar"
+ASSET=$(curl -fsSL "$URL/" | grep -o '/_next/static/[^"]*\.js' | head -1)
+curl -I "$URL$ASSET"
+```
+
+Verify the published UI still targets the local fork contract:
+
+```bash
+rg 'USDCTipJar|address:' packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts
+```
+
+Then start the local fork, deploy, seed USDC, open the IPFS URL, connect a wallet to `http://127.0.0.1:8545` with chain id `31337`, and send a `1 USDC` tip. Confirm the recipient balance changed on the fork:
+
+```bash
+cast call --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545 \
+  0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913 \
+  "balanceOf(address)(uint256)" \
+  0xa0Ee7A142d267C1f36714E4a8F75612F20a79720
+```
